<title>GERMANY: German Q1 GDP up 0.5 pct q/q, 1.4 pct y/y -Stats.</title>
<headline>German Q1 GDP up 0.5 pct q/q, 1.4 pct y/y -Stats.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p>PAN-GERMAN GDP     Q1 97	 Q4 96	  Q3 96</p>
<p> qtr/qtr	     +0.5	   unch	   +0.5</p>
<p> yr/yr		 +1.4	   +1.9	   +2.3</p>
<p>W.GERMAN GDP</p>
<p> yr/yr		 +1.2	   +1.8	   +2.2</p>
<p>E.GERMAN GDP</p>
<p> yr/yr		 +2.8	   +2.8	   +3.4</p>
<p>NOTE - The Federal Statistics Office said the first quarter of 1996 had three fewer workdays than in the year-earlier quarter, which may have over one percentage point from economic growth.</p>
<p>Quarter-on-quarter figures are adjusted for inflation (1991 prices) and for seasonal and calendar factors. They are rounded to a half pct point. Yr/yr changes are adjusted for inflation but not seasonal or calendar factors.  </p>
<p>The Office gave the following yr/yr details:</p>
<p>PAN-GERMAN GDP	     Q1 97	 Q4 96</p>
<p> Private consumption     -0.1	  +1.2</p>
<p> Public consumption	+3.7	  +1.4</p>
<p> Capital investment	+2.2	  +4.1</p>
<p> Construction		+2.3	  +0.6</p>
<p> Exports		     +6.8	  +8.1</p>
<p> Imports		     +3.9	  +4.7</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
